Record and verify archive integrity tags in dependency selections

DUB now records SHA-512 integrity tags for downloaded version dependencies in
$(TT dub.selections.json), and checks them when those dependencies are downloaded
again. Hashes are saved with cached packages so reusing a download or running
$(TT dub upgrade) does not erase its integrity tag. SHA-256 and SHA-384 tags
provided by other tools are also supported.

Existing extracted caches remain trusted and usable without downloading them
again. Entries without recorded hashes gain integrity information on subsequent
downloads. These tags describe the original ZIP bytes; they do not detect later
edits to extracted files. Path and Git dependencies do not acquire archive tags.

Selecting a different version or explicitly upgrading a branch records its new
hash. An unchanged release with a different archive fails verification, including
when the archive is repackaged without changing its extracted contents. Malformed
selections now report an error instead of silently discarding dependency pins.
